EOX is open hardware. Copyright (c) 2026 Zac Elston and EOX contributors.

It is licensed in three parts, by what each file is:

  Hardware design files: CERN-OHL-W-2.0 (CERN Open Hardware Licence v2, weakly reciprocal)
    design/        parameters: models, units, axles, power box, course, ground, trials, reference machines
    bom/           bill of materials

  Software: MIT
    src/  tests/  tools/  pyproject.toml  uv.lock

  Documentation and images: CC-BY-SA-4.0 (Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0)
    README.md  docs/  trials/

The full texts are in LICENSES/. REUSE.toml maps every path to its licence
(https://reuse.software). Files generated from these sources (out/: STEP, DXF,
STL, reports) carry the licence of the sources they come from: CAD and cut
files are hardware design files (CERN-OHL-W-2.0); reports are documentation
(CC-BY-SA-4.0).

Third-party material keeps its own licence: see assets/third_party/ and CREDITS.md.

Source location (CERN-OHL-W-2.0 section 1.10): https://github.com/zacharyelston/EOx
See NOTICE for the notice that must travel with the hardware design files and products made from them.

Versions of EOX published before this change (up to commit 632ed92) were
released under the MIT License, and remain available under it.
